IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `qld-part12a-forms`

-- Tests for Part 12A (qld-part12a-forms.l4).
-- Each expected value was worked out by hand from the text, as cited.

§ `Tests of Part 12A`

#ASSERT `s 48 applies (s 48(1))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48 applies (s 48(1))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the form meets the requirement for a heading (s 48(2))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the form meets the requirement for a heading (s 48(2))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the form meets the requirement for a heading (s 48(2))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3), example 1: forms numbered consecutively starting with the number 1.  Example 2: numbers that reflect the provisions of the Act to which they relate (here sections 5, 12 and 40).
-- src:932 | Examples—
-- src:933 | 1 Forms may be numbered consecutively starting with the number 1.
-- src:934 | 2 Forms may be numbered to reflect the provisions of the Act to which they relate.
@ref s 48(3), examples (src:932-934)
#ASSERT `the forms are numbered using a system that gives each form a unique number (s 48(3))` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the forms are numbered using a system that gives each form a unique number (s 48(3))` (LIST 5, 12, 40) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- SAYS Forms under an authorising law must be numbered so that each form has a unique number, so two forms with the same number do not meet s 48(3).
#ASSERT `the forms are numbered using a system that gives each form a unique number (s 48(3))` (LIST 1, 2, 2) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the forms are numbered using a system that gives each form a unique number (s 48(3))` (LIST 7) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the versions of the form are numbered consecutively using a system that gives each version a unique number (s 48(4))` (LIST 1, 2, 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the versions of the form are numbered consecutively using a system that gives each version a unique number (s 48(4))` (LIST 1, 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the versions of the form are numbered consecutively using a system that gives each version a unique number (s 48(4))` (LIST 2, 2) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the approval or availability of the form is notified as s 48(5) requires (s 48(5))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the approval or availability of the form is notified as s 48(5) requires (s 48(5))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the approval or availability of the form is notified as s 48(5) requires (s 48(5))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6): published in the gazette -- no website date is needed.
#ASSERT `subsection (5) is complied with (s 48(6))` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- published on a website: the date first published must be stated on the website.
#ASSERT `subsection (5) is complied with (s 48(6))` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsection (5) is complied with (s 48(6))` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsection (5) is complied with (s 48(6))` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- nothing published: s 48(6) does not say how else (5) might be complied with
#ASSERT `subsection (5) is complied with (s 48(6))` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `subsection (5) is complied with (s 48(6))` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the requirement for copies to be available is met (s 48(7))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the requirement for copies to be available is met (s 48(7))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the requirement for copies to be available is met (s 48(7))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the failure to comply affects the form's validity (s 48(8))` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the failure to comply affects the form's validity (s 48(8))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the department is the relevant department (s 48(9), definition relevant department)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the department is the relevant department (s 48(9), definition relevant department)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- relevant website: a local government -- only its own website.
#ASSERT `the website is a relevant website (s 48(9), definition relevant website)` TRUE TRUE `the local government's website` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the website is a relevant website (s 48(9), definition relevant website)` TRUE TRUE `the whole-of-government website` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- another entity: the whole-of-government website; the entity's website; if it has none, the relevant department's website or a website identified on it.
#ASSERT `the website is a relevant website (s 48(9), definition relevant website)` FALSE TRUE `the whole-of-government website` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the website is a relevant website (s 48(9), definition relevant website)` FALSE TRUE `the entity's website` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the website is a relevant website (s 48(9), definition relevant website)` FALSE FALSE `the relevant department's website` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the website is a relevant website (s 48(9), definition relevant website)` FALSE TRUE `the relevant department's website` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the website is a relevant website (s 48(9), definition relevant website)` FALSE FALSE `a website identified on the relevant department's website as a website for this purpose` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the website is a relevant website (s 48(9), definition relevant website)` FALSE TRUE `a website identified on the relevant department's website as a website for this purpose` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the website is a relevant website (s 48(9), definition relevant website)` FALSE TRUE `another website` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the website is a relevant website (s 48(9), definition relevant website)` FALSE TRUE `the local government's website` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the website is the whole-of-government website (s 48(9), definition whole-of-government website)` "www.qld.gov.au" FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the website is the whole-of-government website (s 48(9), definition whole-of-government website)` "www.example.com" TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the website is the whole-of-government website (s 48(9), definition whole-of-government website)` "www.example.com" FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 48A`

#ASSERT `strict compliance with the form is necessary (s 48A(1))` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `substantial compliance with the form is sufficient (s 48A(1))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `substantial compliance with the form is sufficient (s 48A(1))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `substantial compliance with the form is sufficient (s 48A(1))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- SAYS A form that requires a specified way of completion, specified information or documents, or verification in a specified way is not properly completed unless the requirement is complied with (s 48A(2)).
#ASSERT `the form is properly completed (s 48A(2))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the form is properly completed (s 48A(2))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the form is properly completed (s 48A(2))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a combined form 1 and 2 may be prescribed or approved and used for the purpose or all the purposes (s 48A(3))` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a combined form 1 and 2 may be prescribed or approved and used for the purpose or all the purposes (s 48A(3))` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4), examples 1 and 2: personal information irrelevant to the purpose, or of some relevance but excessively intrusive, is not reasonably necessary.
-- src:972 | Example 1—
-- src:973 | A prescribed or approved form may not require the provision of personal information irrelevant to a purpose for which the form is required.
-- src:974 | Example 2—
-- src:975 | A prescribed or approved form may not require the provision of personal information that has some relevance to a purpose for which the form is required, but is excessively intrusive to personal privacy.
@ref s 48A(4), examples (src:972-975)
#ASSERT `the form may require the information or documents to be included in, attached to or given with the form (s 48A(4))` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the form may require the information or documents to be included in, attached to or given with the form (s 48A(4))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
